From 8cd3cc5db05f882da9a9f76b2207ed015c2c62ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:32:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] settings_ui: the Agent Sandbox page chooses the vault secrets
 a jail receives
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next §6.53 step 3, the page half of 0207. A Secrets block under
Capabilities lists every vault secret that declares a jail use, one
switch per secret labelled with its variable and hosts
(`GH_TOKEN → github.com, api.github.com`) and noted with its reference.
Turning one on makes the project's list its own, starting from the
default it replaces; a reset button returns to the default, as for the
MCP servers.

A chosen reference the vault cannot hand over -- gone, or declaring no
use -- stays listed, still on, with a note saying why the jail will not
start until it is turned off. While the vault is being read or is
locked the chosen ones show as they are, with no claim they are
missing.

The vault is listed once per page open, not on every settings change:
opening the keyring may ask to unlock it.

The strings are in the nine languages; the seven beyond en-US and
pt-BR are drafts, like the rest of those catalogs.

Tests: agent_jail_secrets_tests.rs -- which secrets are offered, the
missing and no-use notes, and the unread and locked vault.
---

